om Recruitment to Training. Scenario description updated to \\\"Model the impact of training programs\\\". Category adjustments updated with different default values: technical Level Change \\\"+1\\\" and domain Level Change \\\"+1\\\" (vs \\\"0\\\" in Recruitment). Each scenario has distinct configuration.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-10\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Ran Training simulation with default adjustments (Level Change +1 for technical and domain). Model outputs updated: Coverage 78%→91%, Avg Level 3.8→4.5 (Advanced→Expert). Success notification displayed \\\"Simulation Applied - Competency levels and weights have been adjusted\\\". Health alert appeared: \\\"Model Healthy - All competencies are at or above recommended levels with 91% coverage\\\". Reset button visible to restore original state.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-12\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Competency level controls use 5 discrete buttons (one per level 1-5), enforcing the 1-5 range. Product Strategy was at level 4 (Advanced); clicking level button increased it, updating coverage 78%→82%. All weights display in percentage format (e.g., 95%, 80%, 75%) and sliders are present for weight adjustment, indicating 10-100% range. No evidence of values outside constraints in any displayed competency.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-13\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Changed User Research competency level by clicking level button; coverage percentage updated immediately from 78% to 81% and progress indicator updated from 3.8 to 4.0 without requiring reload or any manual refresh action.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-19\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Loaded detail editor and Recruitment tab was initially selected (not requiring manual click). Scenario description visible: \\\\\\\"Simulate candidate profiles and hiring decisions\\\\\\\". Category adjustments initialized: technical (0 competencies), behavioral (1), leadership (1), domain (3) with default level/weight changes of \\\\\\\"0\\\\\\\" and \\\\\\\"0%\\\\\\\". Running simulation without switching tabs applied default Recruitment adjustments to model.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-20\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Increased User Research level via button click. Verified graph still displays current competency node values (e.g., User Research Level: Intermediate, Weight: 75%) and all edges show current weights (90%, 80%, 85%, 70%, 60%). Critical Path updated to 3 competencies. All values matched updated model state. Subsequent edits would operate on new values as demonstrated with level increment starting from 3.8→4.0 result.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-15\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Detail editor displays interactive directed weighted graph: 6 competency nodes (Product Strategy, Prioritization, User Research, Stakeholder Management, Data Analysis, Communication) with relationships shown as arrowed connections with visible weights (90%, 80%, 85%, 70%, 60%). Nodes are draggable, relationships remain attached. Pan, zoom, fit view, toggle interactivity controls visible. React Flow canvas functional.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-16\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Observed critical path recalculation when applying templates and running simulations. Original Product Manager model showed \\\\\\\"4 competencies\\\\\\\" in critical path (Product Strategy, User Research, Communication, +1). After applying HR Manager template, updated to \\\\\\\"3 competencies\\\\\\\" (Talent Acquisition, Employee Relations, HR Compliance). After running Training simulation, critical path values recalculated. Graph display and summary metrics remained consistent with recalculated path.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-17\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Lowered Communication competency (high-weight 90%) level by clicking level button. Immediately created risk-gap: Risk Gaps section changed from \\\\\\\"0 identified\\\\\\\" to \\\\\\\"1 identified\\\\\\\" with \\\\\\\"Communication\\\\\\\" listed. Coverage dropped from 82% to 63%, Avg Level from 4.0 to 3.2. Confirmed that lowering high-weight competency below recommended level triggers immediate risk-gap warning naming the affected competency.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-18\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"After lowering Communication (high-weight 90%) level, prominent \\\\\\\"Competency Gap Alert\\\\\\\" appeared immediately with heading and message: \\\\\\\"1 competency below recommended level: Communication. Consider increasing training focus or adjusting expectations.\\\\\\\" Alert displayed near summary metrics section with icon, confirming system prominently alerts users to risk gaps naming affected competencies and suggesting corrective actions.\"}]}"
